<AddOnInstructionDefinitions Use="Context">
<AddOnInstructionDefinition Use="Target" Name="P_Reset" Revision="3.1" RevisionExtension="01 Release" Vendor="Rockwell Automation" ExecutePrescan="true" ExecutePostscan="false" ExecuteEnableInFalse="true" CreatedDate="2008-08-19T20:03:31.976Z" CreatedBy="Not Available" EditedDate="2014-09-03T14:38:47.522Z"
 EditedBy="PROCESS\Library" SoftwareRevision="v18.02">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Reset]]>
</Description>
<RevisionNote>
<![CDATA[See V3.1-xx Release Notes for details. Unmodified, up-rev only for V3.1-01 public release.]]>
</RevisionNote>
<AdditionalHelpText>
<![CDATA[Copyright © Rockwell Automation, Inc.  All Rights Reserved.

This instruction provides a central point in a control strategy (CM, EM, Unit, Group, Cell, Area, etc.)
or controller for accepting and fanning out a Reset of equipment alarms and faults.

Resets are accepted from Program Command (PCmd_Reset), Operator Command (OCmd_Reset) or
as an Input from another object (Inp_Reset).  The input can be tied to the output of a higher-level
Reset instruction to cascade Resets down through a hierarchy, say from a master Station Reset
to individual groups or units.

The minimum duration of the reset Output is configurable.  This can be set to allow time for a
Reset sent to equipment via an output card to feed back into the system via inputs.

The P_Reset instruction can be used on a ladder rung with the rung condition transitioning
from FALSE to TRUE causing the output to pulse.  In this configuration, the Program and
Operator Commands and the reset Input still function normally, even if the rung is FALSE.]]>
</AdditionalHelpText>
<Parameters>
<Parameter Name="EnableIn" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Input" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false" ExternalAccess="Read Only">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Enable Input - System Defined Parameter]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="EnableOut" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false" ExternalAccess="Read Only">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Enable Output - System Defined Parameter]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Inp_Reset" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Input" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="true" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Reset Input, 1=Reset, from pushbutton or another object]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Inp_ResetReqd" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Input" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="true" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[1=Reset Required, enable Reset button]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>01</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="1"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Cfg_MinHoldTime" TagType="Base" DataType="DINT" Usage="Input" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Minimum Time to hold Reset Output true (sec)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>01 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="1"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="PCmd_Reset" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Input" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Program Command to Reset, from other object]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="OCmd_Reset" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Input" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Operator Command to Reset, from HMI]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Out_Reset" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="true" ExternalAccess="Read Only">
<Description>
<![CDATA[1=Reset received for this P_Reset's scope]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Sts_Err" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="true" ExternalAccess="Read Only">
<Description>
<![CDATA[1=Error in Config: Invalid Hold Time (use 0 to 2147483)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Rdy_Reset" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false" ExternalAccess="Read Only">
<Description>
<![CDATA[1=Ready to receive OCmd_Reset (enable button)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>01</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="1"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="P_Reset" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Unique Parameter Name for auto - discovery]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
</Parameters>
<LocalTags>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_HoldT" DataType="TIMER" ExternalAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Reset Output Hold Timer (TOF)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<Structure DataType="TIMER">
<DataValueMember Name="PRE" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="ACC" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="EN" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="TT" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="DN" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_EnableInONS" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[EnableIn transition detection to pulse Reset Output]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>01</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="1"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_HoldONS" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[One-Shot to fire Hold Timer to ensure min. output ON time.]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_ResetCond" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Any incoming Reset condition is TRUE]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Inf_Type" DataType="STRING_16" ExternalAccess="Read Only">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Type identifier for HMI navigation]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>07 00 00 00 50 5F 52 65 73 65 74 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="String" Length="7">
<![CDATA['P_Reset']]>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Cfg_Tag" DataType="STRING_20" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Tagname for display on HMI]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>07 00 00 00 50 5F 52 65 73 65 74 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="String" Length="7">
<![CDATA['P_Reset']]>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Cfg_Label" DataType="STRING_20" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Label for graphic symbol displayed on HMI]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>05 00 00 00 52 65 73 65 74 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="String" Length="5">
<![CDATA['Reset']]>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Cfg_Desc" DataType="STRING_40" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Description for display on HMI]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>15 00 00 00 4D 75 6C 74 69 70 6C 65 2D 44 65 76 
69 63 65 20 52 65 73 65 74 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="String" Length="21">
<![CDATA['Multiple-Device Reset']]>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Inf_Lib" DataType="STRING_12" ExternalAccess="Read Only">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Display Library for Faceplate call-up]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>06 00 00 00 52 41 2D 42 41 53 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="String" Length="6">
<![CDATA['RA-BAS']]>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
</LocalTags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="EnableInFalse" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Sets up for One-Shot trigger of Reset using XIC/XIO on rung]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
P_Reset:  RESET EnableIn False Handling
============================================================
On EnableIn False:

Clear the bit used to detect EnableIn transition from False to True
in preparation for the next transition

(See main Logic Routine for EnableIn False-to-True triggering of Reset.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Wrk_EnableInONS);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
CONFIGURATION
============================================================
This rung takes the configured Output Hold time and calculates
the appropriate hold timer preset.  A negative preset would fault
the controller and so is disallowed.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MUL(Cfg_MinHoldTime,1000,Wrk_HoldT.PRE)XIC(Wrk_HoldT.PRE.31)CLR(Wrk_HoldT.PRE)OTE(Sts_Err);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
COMMAND AND INPUT HANDLING
============================================================
This rung processes received Reset Commands from:

1.  Higher-level strategies via Program Command
2.  The Operator via HMI Operator Command
3.  Pushbuttons or other block via Input, or
4.  On transition of rung condition from False to True
(button or other logic as rung condition).

The reset starts the Hold Timer (One-Shot Off-Delay)
to ensure the output is held on for at least the minimum time.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(PCmd_Reset) OTU(PCmd_Reset) ,XIC(OCmd_Reset) OTU(OCmd_Reset) ,XIC(Inp_Reset) ][OTE(Wrk_ResetCond) ,ONS(Wrk_HoldONS) TOF(Wrk_HoldT,?,?) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Hold Timer "done" bit comes on immediately and stays on
for the hold time.  If it, or any held-on reset initiator, is TRUE, set the Output.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_HoldT.DN) ,XIC(Wrk_ResetCond) ]OTE(Out_Reset);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If an associated object is ready to be reset, set the Inp_Reset pin on this object.
Then, if something needs reset, and we're not already resetting it, enable this
object's Reset Pushbutton.

(If this function is not wired, the button will generally be enabled.
If this function IS wired, it is suggested to make the enabled Reset button
FLASH to alert the operator that a reset is required!)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Inp_ResetReqd)XIO(Out_Reset)OTE(Rdy_Reset);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Process Reset Input and Commands]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Copyright © Rockwell Automation, Inc.  All Rights Reserved.
============================================================
P_Reset:  PROCESS -- RESET
============================================================
Revision 3.1-01 Release  2014-09-03:  See V3.1-xx Release Notes for details.
V1.x, V2.x Revision History archived.
V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Inf_Lib. Added display of Local STRING Tags
on header (this) rung.
V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Unmodified for Library of Process Objects V3.1, up-rev only.
V3.1-01  2014-09-03:  Unmodified, up-rev only for V3.1-01 public release.
============================================================
This Instruction provides a command/interface point for resetting
alarms, faults or other conditions across a strategy (EM,
Unit, Cell, Area, Site, etc.).  Its Output is intended to be wired
to input, device and interlock instructions to allow a single reset
command or pushbutton to reset alarms and faults in all objects in its scope.
============================================================
POWERUP OR INVALID STATE
============================================================
No special powerup logic is required.

============================================================
SHOW LOCAL STRINGS
============================================================
The STRINGs containing the text associated with each instance of this
instruction cannot be Input or Output Parameters, because STRINGs are not
 'atomic' types. (Inputs and Outputs must be SINT, INT, DINT, REAL, or BOOL.)

In order to make it easier to find and configure these STRINGs, this rung
was added.  THE JMP (and the LBL on the following rung)
MUST NOT BE REMOVED!!!

To view the STRINGs, go to the instruction instance (in LD or FBD), RIGHT-click
to bring up the context menu and select "Open Instruction Logic".
This rung will appear with the STRING values for the selected instance.
You may double-click the STRING values here to modify them as well.

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added rung to show strings  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[JMP(SkipText)CONCAT(Cfg_Desc,Cfg_Label,Cfg_Tag)LOWER(Inf_Lib,Inf_Type);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
CONFIGURATION
============================================================
This rung takes the configured Output Hold time and calculates
the appropriate hold timer preset.  A negative preset would fault
the controller and so is disallowed and flagged.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(SkipText)MUL(Cfg_MinHoldTime,1000,Wrk_HoldT.PRE)XIC(Wrk_HoldT.PRE.31)CLR(Wrk_HoldT.PRE)OTE(Sts_Err);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
COMMAND AND INPUT HANDLING
============================================================
This rung processes received Reset Commands from:

1.  Higher-level strategies via Program Command
2.  The Operator via HMI Operator Command
3.  Pushbuttons or other block via Input, or
4.  On transition of rung condition from False to True
(button or other logic as rung condition).

The reset starts the Hold Timer (One-Shot Off-Delay)
to ensure the output is held on for at least the minimum time.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(PCmd_Reset) OTU(PCmd_Reset) ,XIC(OCmd_Reset) OTU(OCmd_Reset) ,XIC(Inp_Reset) ,XIO(Wrk_EnableInONS) OTL(Wrk_EnableInONS) ][OTE(Wrk_ResetCond) ,ONS(Wrk_HoldONS) TOF(Wrk_HoldT,?,?) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Hold Timer "done" bit comes on immediately and stays on
for the hold time.  If it, or any held-on reset initiator, is TRUE, set the Output.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_HoldT.DN) ,XIC(Wrk_ResetCond) ]OTE(Out_Reset);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If an associated object is ready to be reset, set the Inp_Reset pin on this object.
Then, if something needs reset, and we're not already resetting it, enable this
object's Reset Pushbutton.

(If this function is not wired, the button will generally be enabled.
If this function IS wired, it is suggested to make the enabled Reset button
FLASH to alert the operator that a reset is required!)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Inp_ResetReqd)XIO(Out_Reset)OTE(Rdy_Reset);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Prescan" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Clear "lurking" Commands]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
PRESCAN (POWERUP) HANDLING
============================================================
On Prescan, clear any "lurking" Commands.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(OCmd_Reset)OTU(PCmd_Reset);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
<Dependencies>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_40"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_20"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_12"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_16"/>
</Dependencies>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
</AddOnInstructionDefinitions>
</Controller>
